From f3f9a00baeb53a75cc4136f2915d04faac94c7b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 01:57:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 22/29] rewrite(remap-emitter-regression): test the current
 custom_adapter short-circuit, not the retired typed body

synth/remap:remap became corpus-status "adapter" (typed generation cannot
be bit-exact against the authority for this program -- see
remap_profile.py's module docstring) and emit_typed_cpp.render_typed_cpp
now special-cases REMAP_KEY before ever constructing an _Emitter: it
unconditionally returns a fixed "custom_adapter route" comment naming
noisemaker::effects::bind_remap, ignoring remap_profile/
remap_frontend_proof entirely (verified directly: render_typed_cpp
returns the byte-identical stub whether called with no profile, a real
authenticated profile+proof, a proof with no profile, a foreign-key or
truncated-index proof, or an unrecognized profile string).

The old test_remap_emitter_regression.py asserted the OPPOSITE of all of
this: that an authenticated profile+proof caused a typed body
(RemapUniformData, remap_data_index, ...) to be emitted, and that a
missing/foreign/stale profile or proof caused render_typed_cpp to raise
TypedEmissionError. Both premises are gone by design -- rule 4 territory
(a test targeting removed behavior gets replaced with a test of the
current design, not deleted). It also inherited the same wrong-corpus-
source bug as test_remap_frontend_profile.py (reading the live 0ed489ec
remap.glsl against remap_profile.py's OLD-corpus-pinned RAW_SHA256),
which is why 3 of its 4 old tests ERRORed before ever reaching the
behavior they meant to check.

Replaced with five tests pinning the actual current contract: the stub
renders with no profile at all, and is not bypassable by a real,
profile-less, foreign, stale, or wrong-string profile/proof -- there is
nothing left to admit or fail closed on for this key's typed body.
Kept the corrected (a024dc3a) corpus source for building the historical
proof object itself, matching test_remap_frontend_profile.py. All 5
tests pass (Ran 5 tests ... OK).

